From: Harbourline scenarios <scenarios@harbourline.test>
Subject: [PATCH] db: relax orders.currency ahead of multi-currency carts

Drops the NOT NULL default on orders.currency so the upcoming multi-currency
cart can decide the currency later. Looks harmless in review; in production
the fulfilment worker reads order.currency on every new order and crashes on
NULL (seed-spec planted_edge_cases → bad-migration). Labs 2 and 12 apply it
with `git apply scenarios/bad-migration.patch`; `scenarios/lab-reset.sh`
reverts it with `git apply -R`.
---
 db/migrations/1761094800000_orders-currency-nullable.sql | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 db/migrations/1761094800000_orders-currency-nullable.sql

diff --git a/db/migrations/1761094800000_orders-currency-nullable.sql b/db/migrations/1761094800000_orders-currency-nullable.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b2f8e3c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/db/migrations/1761094800000_orders-currency-nullable.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+-- Up Migration
+-- "Prepare orders for multi-currency carts": the currency will be decided at payment time.
+-- Reviewer note: this is the planted bad migration (scenarios/bad-migration.patch).
+-- The worker dereferences order.currency on every new order and dies on NULL.
+ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN currency DROP DEFAULT;
+ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN currency DROP NOT NULL;
+
+-- Down Migration
+UPDATE orders SET currency = 'USD' WHERE currency IS NULL;
+ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN currency SET NOT NULL;
+ALTER TABLE orders ALTER COLUMN currency SET DEFAULT 'USD';
+
--
2.43.0
